text:
alex: Heads-up: integrating embeddings+rerank in the new sampleapp uncovered SDK parity issues across Node and Python. Node's batching helper sometimes yields extra nesting for single-item batches and the rerank response field name varies by model version. Also seeing duplicate processing when auth retries.

priya: Curious — can you paste a tiny repro and a server response?

alex: Yep, minimal repro and examples below. Short version: Node helper returns [[...]] for n=1, Python returns [...]. Rerank responses alternate between \"score\" and \"ranking_score\" depending on model.

```
// Node (sampleapp helper)
const batch = makeEmbedBatch([{text: 'hello'}]);
console.log(batch.length) // 1
console.log(Array.isArray(batch[0])) // true  // -> nested vector
// API response: { data: [[0.01,0.02,...]] }

# Python
b = make_batch(['hello'])
# b -> [0.01,0.02,...] (flat)

// Rerank example from hosted:
{ "results": [{ "id": "doc1", "ranking_score": 0.74 }] }
// but other runs: { "results": [{ "id": "doc1", "score": 0.74 }] }
```

nate: I can repro the Node nesting. Looks like the helper wraps outputs irrespective of the downstream expectation when batchSize === 1. Quick fix: normalize at the helper boundary or ensure helper always returns list-of-list and Python helper does same.

emily: On the rerank field: we should accept both keys in SDK mapping to avoid breaking apps when model updates change field names. Fallback order: score, ranking_score, confidence.

alex: Bonus problem: our Node auth middleware retries 401s by re-sending the entire request but drops the x-rw-client-id header used for idempotency. Server ends up processing twice for some side-effecting endpoints.

priya: Workarounds:
- Client-side normalize embeddings shape before passing to retriever (ensure list-of-list).
- Map rerank keys with fallback.
- Add a client-generated idempotency header preserved across retries.

Example snippet I used in sampleapp:

```js
// normalize embeddings
let e = resp.data;
if (!Array.isArray(e[0])) e = [e];

// score fallback
const mapped = res.results.map(r => ({ id: r.id, score: r.score ?? r.ranking_score ?? r.confidence }));
```

ci-bot: Created ticket DEVEX-2610: \"SDK parity: embed batch shape + rerank field variance + auth retry idempotency\". Linked PRs requested: node-helper-fix, sdk-score-fallback, auth-retry-preserve-id. Please attach e2e parity test in sampleapp that compares normalized outputs across both SDKs.

nate: I'll open the node-helper PR today to ensure consistent shape for single-item batches and add unit tests. Emily, can you spearhead the SDK mapping change?

emily: Yup, will push a small mapping patch and add JSON schema for rerank responses to catch regressions.

alex: Thanks all. Once PRs land, I'll update the sampleapp template and the onboarding blurb so new users don't hit this. :sparkles:
